[step] Required raised identification lettering: the flush fitting face is nativeY 2 and the contrasting word stands 0.48 mm above it in two 0.24 mm layers. This is the named two-colour letter feature, not an accidental change of wall plane. The earlier TAP/FLAVOR appearance record accepts the raised-letter process, not the smaller current type or mounting fit.
alternatives: Flush two-colour text would remove the raised mark. Raising by 3 mm would put lettering far above the fitting face and change the selected label interface. The retained 0.48 mm mark uses the shared label process; this answer does not establish small-type print quality.
