alternatives: Three-millimetre glyph strokes would close the letter counters. Enlarging the shared 6.5 mm type within the fixed band reduces clearance to the bulkhead flange and upper edge; flattening the word removes the raised mark. This answer is limited to the actual glyph points, and gives no strength or lifetime result.
